# Line-ending and encoding contract for this repository.
#
# Root cause this fixes: with no .gitattributes, Git fell back to the ambient
# machine default core.autocrlf=true, which silently converts LF->CRLF on checkout
# and CRLF->LF on commit. Tools that bypass the smudge filter (git apply, raw file
# writes, piped patches) then see LF while the working tree carries CRLF, producing
# phantom whole-file diffs and mis-staged hunks. An explicit contract makes EOL
# deterministic regardless of machine or tool.
#
# Policy: text is auto-detected and normalized to LF in the repository. Windows
# script shells that genuinely require CRLF to run keep CRLF on checkout.
# Binary assets are declared so they are never subject to text conversion.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts that must keep CRLF to execute reliably.
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf

# Binary formats: never treat as text, never convert line endings.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf  binary
*.pbix binary
*.zip  binary
